   "gap": "Supply the complete entry for Wald's second identity with all of the source's hypotheses: the statement (handbook/parts/p15/optional-stopping-and-random-walks.tex lines 170-192, thm:p15-os-wald-second) asserts S_{T and n} -> S_T in L2 and ES_T^2 = sigma^2 ET for any T with ET<infinity without stating that T is a stopping time, whereas held source Exercise 4.8.4 (Durrett v5, printed p. 261 = PDF p. 269) requires 'T is a stopping time with ET<infinity' and the annex proof (annex line 186) uses that {T>=j} is F_{j-1}-measurable. The identity fails without the hypothesis (fair signs, T=1 on {xi_1=xi_2}, T=2 otherwise: ES_T^2=1/2, sigma^2 ET=3/2). The unstated assumption must be supplied so the source hypothesis is preserved; the exit-time bound, its strict form and the sigma^2=0 case are present.",
